  "manifest_sha256": "7294e3edcd3468aeb8881182f77a3f22c9d9de41dff1dba8f183e9fe1753c9a7",
  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nHow many patients can the hospital admit per week during the outbreak? Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 55 patients are admitted into the hospital each day. During the outbreak, the hospital's weekly patient-admission report is reviewed by the hospital's administrative office. The report categorizes admitted patients by department, such as emergency medicine, pediatrics, and surgery. The hospital uses an electronic registration system to record each patient's admission date.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "EXACT PUBLIC STATE AFTER TURN 1; NO PRIVATE OR FUTURE DATA\nPUBLIC_STATE_JSON:\n{\"completed_task_turns\":[{\"turn\":1,\"user_message\":\"Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\\\boxed{}.\\n\\nHow many patients can the hospital admit per week during the outbreak? Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 55 patients are admitted into the hospital each day. During the outbreak, the hospital's weekly patient-admission report is reviewed by the hospital's administrative office. The report categorizes admitted patients by department, such as emergency medicine, pediatrics, and surgery. The hospital uses an electronic registration system to record each patient's admission date.\"}],\"public_metadata\":{\"benchmark\":\"Evolving Intent GSM8K\",\"upstream_commit\":\"993d6be9597ac03854b46362ccd647eb1bfd267a\"}}",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Due to the coronavirus outbreak, 50 patients are admitted into the hospital each day.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "A week has 7 days, and 50 patients are admitted each day.\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 7 = 350\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the hospital can admit\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{350}\n\\]\n\npatients per week.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How many beds does the hospital need to handle its daily admissions for one week? Additionally, here are some details: the hospital's admissions office is open seven days during the week. Each daily admission requires one completed intake form before the patient is assigned to a bed.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital admits 50 patients each day for 7 days:\n\n\\[\n50 \\times 7 = 350\n\\]\n\nSince each patient needs one bed after completing the intake form, the hospital needs:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{350\\text{ beds}}\n\\]\n\nassuming each bed is needed for the entire week.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "I should also tell you: the hospital has a capacity of 1050 beds.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital needs to accommodate:\n\n\\[\n50 \\text{ patients/day} \\times 7 \\text{ days} = 350 \\text{ beds}\n\\]\n\nWith a capacity of 1,050 beds, it has:\n\n\\[\n1050 - 350 = 700\n\\]\n\nbeds remaining. Therefore, the hospital has enough capacity, with **700 beds to spare**.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Okay, now can you extend that? Specifically: How many unoccupied beds are in the hospital after 2 weeks? One more thing you should know: One-fifth of the hospital beds are occupied.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "The hospital has \\(1{,}050\\) beds, and initially one-fifth are occupied:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1050=210\\text{ occupied beds}\n\\]\n\nOver 2 weeks, the hospital admits:\n\n\\[\n50\\times 14=700\\text{ patients}\n\\]\n\nAssuming no patients are discharged, the total occupied beds after 2 weeks are:\n\n\\[\n210+700=910\n\\]\n\nThus, the number of unoccupied beds is:\n\n\\[\n1050-910=\\boxed{140}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "One more thing — The time period is 2 weeks.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since the time period is 2 weeks:\n\n1. Initial occupied beds:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1050=210\n\\]\n\n2. New admissions over 2 weeks:\n\\[\n50\\times 7\\times 2=700\n\\]\n\n3. Total occupied beds:\n\\[\n210+700=910\n\\]\n\n4. Unoccupied beds:\n\\[\n1050-910=\\boxed{140}\n\\]\n\nSo, assuming no patients are discharged, **140 beds remain unoccupied after 2 weeks**.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. The hospital has a capacity of 1000 beds.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "With a capacity of \\(1{,}000\\) beds:\n\n1. Initially occupied beds:\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{5}\\times 1000=200\n\\]\n\n2. Admissions over 2 weeks:\n\\[\n50\\times 14=700\n\\]\n\n3. Total occupied beds:\n\\[\n200+700=900\n\\]\n\n4. Unoccupied beds:\n\\[\n1000-900=\\boxed{100}\n\\]\n\nAssuming no patients are discharged, **100 beds remain unoccupied after 2 weeks**.",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
